ys maintained you  know this might be the exception this  year I've always said that the team that  can utilize their starters more and the  long-run has a better chance to win it  all  but what Milwaukee did in the short  series winning three games they were  able to have that formula proved  successful so if they can continue to do  that and win an extraordinary x' and not  have serious drag on then I think they  got a great chance  the Dodgers lineup with relentless their  bench is as good as anybody so they can  mix and match it's just a matter of how  does Dave Roberts stay patient and not  right away when you know they make a lot  of changes and go to the bullpen it's  got to pick and choose where he's going  to use guys off the bench  Clayton Clayton Kershaw's regular season  ER a is the lowest among pitchers with  at least 200 starts since 1920 his four  point career postseason er a is the  second highest among those with at least  15 starts second second only to CC  Sabathia did you see anything in his  last start that would kind of put your  fears to rest if you're a Dodger fan of  what you expect from Clayton Kershaw who  does pitch well at Miller Park yeah you  know the perception of course has been  he had those four kind of crazy games I  think three of them against st. Louis in  the last year's game against the Astros  that might stick out but the Dodgers of  won ten of his last eleven or ten of his  last 12 postseason starts so to me that  that that speaks to how he has adjusted  and last game he showed that he can  pitch without 95 he only struck out one  guy which is like one of the first times  in a long time that he's ever done that  if ever and I think this series knowing  that he has been rested and that he has  been taken care of as he doesn't have to  be the Bulldog all year look his mindset  still give me the ball I'm the best  pitcher in the universe that's what you  got to have but the team has recognized  that you know the depth of the rotate  allows them to not have to have kershaw  come on three days rest like you did a  lot of times in those past past post  season so I maintain that's in the  rearview mirror for him and  statistically I think you'll see that  come down and be more reflective of his  regular season  Fox Sports opens its coverage to the  national championship series between the  Dodgers Brewers tonight from Miller Park  pregame will be at 7:00 Eastern on Fox  Sports one game coverage at 8:00 Eastern  on Fox Sports one Jill buck John and Ken  Rosenthal Tom Verducci will be there on  the call Game two from Milwaukee or  Saturday afternoon at 4:00 live on Fox  Network how do you not let ego factor in  when you're on the mound it can be hard  especially when you start thinking about  let's just say last series  what Kershaw doing start Game one you  know there are things that in this game  that when you have a reputation or when  you are the best pitcher in baseball for  the last 10 11 years and guys in your  club you know stuff is starting to be a  little bit better if you'd better look  to me I think what Clayton represents is  everything we want a player to represent  so at times an organization may have to  have conversations or communication  since with your star player but the ego  on the mound has got to be there in the  ability to think that you are better  than anybody that steps in the plate but  you can't allow it to have such a chip  on your shoulder and that's easier said  that done when you may be passed over or  somebody else might be the hotter  pitcher at the time and that's just a  unique situation that the Dodgers have  have so many good pictures that they get  to line it up the way they get to line  it up Christian Yelich is 9 for 17  against Kershaw  so he's batting 529 there were certain  guys that had your number do you change  anything because of that success that  they have against you  yeah I think you know the tree if it  were the regular season you you look 