an  anybody being able to come up with that  big hit or just something small moving a  runner over getting a runner in from  third it just didn't feel like the  Yankees were built that way you know we  see a lot of teams that are like this  though John  so I wonder where we're there there is a  place for that in baseball and how  important and I feel like it there's  something going to happen in this  postseason whether it's the championship  series or the World Series we're  something small will decide who wins it  all I really believe that and we get  caught up in strikeouts in homeruns and  it still feels like there's nuance here  that you know some of these teams don't  factor in your thoughts on them  absolutely no absolutely and I've gone  back 10 years I mean eventually if  everyone starts flying closer to the  same type of baseball someone's going to  win the World Series leading the league  in the home runs but it rarely happens I  mean you got to go back forever  that you got teams that lead the league  in homeruns and are up there and  strikeouts it just it just doesn't bode  well for a championship run but if you  do take your walks and you get on base  and you put pressure on the pitchers you  have a better chance look last year was  a great example of the Houston Astros  getting those strikeouts making the  contact doing the little things that's  what allows them to win the World Series  now what's gonna always stand out is the  big home runs you know springers home  runs home runs still a reign king in our  game from a standpoint of instant runs  and they're just harder or typically  they were harder to come by in the  postseason because you're facing elite  pitchers but when every guy in the  lineup now or the potential of guys  hitting home runs are in the lineups  you're gonna run into more of those so  that's gonna still stick out but I still  totally agree with you that the team  with the least amount of selfish at-bats  and I'm talking about a selfish if that  to me is defined as running around third  less than two outs and you're still  trying to hit a home run when the  infields back and all you got to do is  hit a ground ball to get the game closer  or tie it up you know those are the  things that if you still have too many  of those selfish bats in your club  you're gonna have to be so much better  than the other team to win because  you're given you're just not putting  yourself in the best situation so I  totally totally agree with that  statement and and as time goes on we'll  see if a team can defy that on a year  where they  win it all and they you know they led  the postseason and strikeouts and they  let the postseason and it just it it's  going to come down to that and and  that's what I'm always looking forward  to see which player is able to do that  or which team is able to do that better  good to talk to you John have fun  tonight and we'll catch up with you soon  thank you you got a dad that's a John  Smoltz Hall of Famer and working for Fox  as their baseball analyst in the  postseason coverage tonight 7:00 Eastern  on Fox Sports 1  and then the game at 8 o'clock on Fox  Sports 1 Joe Buck John Smoltz Kenny  Rosenthal Tom Verducci and then game 2  will be Saturday afternoon at 4:00 on  Fox for more Dan Patrick show to the  audience channel 239 on DirecTV or  download the Dan Patrick show app  [Music]

